# Normalise line endings to LF, in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# This checkout lives on the Linux filesystem and is read by PHP there, but is
# also committed through SourceTree on Windows over \\wsl$\. Git for Windows
# defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which wrote CRLF into the Linux tree and made
# 20 of the 30 tracked files show as modified with no real change. The ten that
# stayed clean are the _output/phrases/*.txt files - one line, no terminator,
# nothing for a Windows client to rewrite.
#
#   text=auto  store LF in the repository, whatever the committing platform does
#   eol=lf     check LF back out, so core.autocrlf on the Windows side cannot
#              reintroduce CRLF on disk
#
# Every tracked file here is text (PHP, JSON, Markdown, phrases), so one blanket
# rule covers the repository.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Guard the binary types an add-on may later ship (icons, screenshots) against
# being mangled by the rule above. None are tracked today.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.webp binary
*.zip  binary

# Keep development-only files out of `git archive` output - GitHub's "Download ZIP".
# This is one of three separate exclusion surfaces and covers none of the others:
#   the git repo        -> .gitignore       (CLAUDE.local.md)
#   git archive output  -> here
#   the XenForo zip     -> build.json `rm`  (the builder walks the filesystem, not git)
/CLAUDE.md        export-ignore
/CLAUDE.local.md  export-ignore
/TESTING.md       export-ignore
/tests            export-ignore
/phpunit.xml      export-ignore
/composer.json    export-ignore
/composer.lock    export-ignore
/.gitattributes   export-ignore
/.gitignore       export-ignore
